# =============================================================================
# ATLAS ASCEND — environment
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. Set the same values in the Vercel
# dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment Variables) for deployment.
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. Never commit a real token.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONLY REQUIRED VARIABLE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mapbox public access token — must start with `pk.`
# Create at https://account.mapbox.com/access-tokens/
#
# This is the SINGLE source of truth for the browser map. It is read in exactly
# one place — `getMapboxToken()` in src/lib/env.ts — and nothing else in the
# application supplies a token to Mapbox GL JS.
#
# It ships to the browser by design (that is what NEXT_PUBLIC_ means). Protect
# it with URL restrictions in the Mapbox dashboard, not by hiding it.
#
# REQUIRED SCOPES — if you created a dedicated token and unchecked any boxes,
# these are the ones the map actually needs:
#   • styles:tiles  — vector tile requests (mapbox.mapbox-streets-v8).
#                     WITHOUT THIS THE MAP RENDERS EMPTY/BLACK.
#   • fonts:read    — glyph ranges for map labels. Without it, labels vanish
#                     but geography still draws.
#   • styles:read   — NOT required. atlasNight is authored in this repository,
#                     so no Mapbox-hosted style is ever fetched.
#
# Without this variable the app still runs and shows an explicit
# "Map service not configured" state rather than a blank canvas.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL — you almost certainly do not need this
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A separate server-only token used ONLY by /api/search for geocoding.
#
# THIS VARIABLE HAS NO EFFECT ON THE MAP. If it is set in Vercel and you are
# debugging a blank map, it is a red herring — delete it.
#
# It exists for one narrow reason: geocoding is billed per request, so you may
# eventually want it on a separately-scoped, separately-rotatable token that
# never reaches the browser. Until you want that, leave it unset —
# /api/search falls back to NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN automatically.
# MAPBOX_TOKEN=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT YET USED — reserved for a later phase
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Atlas natural-language intelligence. Until this is set, Atlas runs on its
# deterministic rule set only and says so rather than improvising.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Persistence. Vehicles and destinations are currently stored in the browser
# only. See ARCHITECTURE.md for the intended Postgres + auth setup.
# DATABASE_URL=
